ops.body:
Routed the root scheduler review FAIL (reviews/scheduler.json @ b55d73a: Stop hang, because the synchronous scan never sees cancellation). Fix Run wf_dc16734e-245 on branch cc-sync/scheduler-stopfix from b55d73a, diff confined to internal/scheduler:
- Stop cancels the work context directly before waiting;
- regression tests (failing first) for Stop during a blocking initial, periodic and Kick-triggered scan and during an in-flight capture, plus Stop-before-Run and double Stop;
- -race -count=5, then astra verification and a refix.
It merges into cc-sync/integration in phase 2b.
D15 scope clarification adopted into doc 64803ab: no compatibility or migrations for unreleased intermediate cache/ledger formats (the 76e7ece cache blocker). Instead a clean versioned v1 cache/ledger that invalidates anything else. Same-final-version attribute-change reclassification stays correct. The final reposync merge reconciles the D15 fixes with the overlapping 3ea2d6b fixes rather than duplicating them, and removes any intermediate-cache compatibility code.
reposync delta Run wf_0bc0f2e7-c46 is complete: cc-sync/worktree-delta @ fd46c690e90b. It merges root fixes + stamp, adds D14 (submodule filter env, hidden-flag WIP incl. assume-unchanged/skip-worktree edits/deletes/chmod with flags re-applied, jj @-tracked ignored files), then the astra review fix, where all 5 findings were real and fixed with failing-first tests:
- hidden intent-to-add;
- flagged submodules now omitted and stamped;
- sparse check-rules gating so real deletions of included paths are captured;
- jj-workspace submodule filters;
- GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1 in ReadOnlyGitEnv.
Coordinator decisions (D14 addendum in 64803ab):
- An intent-to-add path deleted on disk is captured and restored exactly (option a).
- Minimum git is 2.44 on every host (typed preflight error, documented).
- Honest limit: hidden flags inside a submodule make that submodule look clean.
